text:
lin: Quick ticket from a new user: sampleapp logs show `request_id: <redacted>` during OTEL auto-instrument startup. They said they followed the quickstart unchanged.

alex: Do we have the sample app middleware ordering documented? OTEL auto-instrumentation can inject wrappers that alter req/res prototypes.

lin: Minimal repro they pasted: 
```js
const otel = require('@opentelemetry/auto-instrument');
const express = require('express');
const requestId = require('express-request-id')();
const app = express();
app.use(otel()); // auto-instrument first
app.use(requestId); // user put this after otel
app.use(require('./log-middleware')());
app.get('/ok', (_,res) => res.end('ok'));
```
They observe header present on incoming call but logs show dash. Moving requestId before otel fixes it.

piper: Two possible culprits: 1) OTEL wrapper replaces request instance and our log middleware reads the wrong object, 2) redact middleware ran earlier and stripped x-request-id header under STRICT mode.

alex: Right — we've seen the double-race: ordering + redact. Quick mitigation: make log-middleware attempt several fallbacks: req.requestId, req.headers['x-request-id'], res.getHeader('x-request-id'), and if OTEL present, check the active span attributes.

lin: Sketch I sent: 
```js
function pickId(req, res){
  if (req && req.requestId) return req.requestId;
  if (req && req.headers && req.headers['x-request-id']) return req.headers['x-request-id'];
  try{ const span = require('@opentelemetry/api').trace.getSpan(require('@opentelemetry/api').context.active()); if (span && span.attributes) return span.attributes['http.request_id'] || span.attributes['x-request-id']; }catch(e){}
  if (res && res.getHeader) return res.getHeader('x-request-id');
  return '-';
}
```
This handles wrapped reqs.

security: If we surface header values in logs we must ensure PII controls hold. Proposal: add REDACT_ALLOWLIST_HEADERS to default include x-request-id and a HASH_REQID toggle so logs only contain HMAC(id).

piper: Small hotfix plan: 1) patch log-middleware fallback (unit test covering OTEL-wrapped req) 2) add REDACT_ALLOWLIST_HEADERS env support and documentation 3) add HASH_REQID option that runs HMAC with service key when enabled.

alex: Also add onboarding note: "If you enable OTEL auto-instrumentation, register request-id middleware before auto-instrument or enable REDACT_ALLOWLIST_HEADERS+HASH_REQID to retain stable correlators."

lin: I'll open a tiny PR for the fallback and add a reproducible unit test that simulates replaceable req object and REDACT_STRICT mode. If security wants the HMAC helper we can share the KMS-backed key usage pattern.

security: Ack. We prefer hashing in prod; add a privacy doc snippet. Ensure HASH_REQID default is off for OSS.

deploy-bot: lin opened PR #5077: "log-middleware: resilient request id resolution across OTEL + redact allowlist support"  CI queued.

alex: Nice. Also adding an integration note to the sampleapp README so first-run users don't hit this surprise.

lin: Thanks — will follow up with PR link in onboarding ticket. :thumbsup:
